# Build quiz question extraction into course-sync

## Step

Teach course-sync to derive `question` content resources from inline
`QuizQuestion` markup. Execution is authorized (brief Notes, Joel 2026-07-24).
Decided in
[Decide what identifies an inline quiz](./decide-inline-quiz-identity.svx).

This is the load-bearing piece of the architecture: it is what makes quiz data
queryable and what lets the server grade authoritatively, while leaving Matt's
authoring entirely inline.

**Follow the existing pattern, do not invent a parallel one.** Sync already mints
deterministic ids as
`sync_${kind}_${sha256(bindingId:kind:sourceId).slice(0,24)}`
(`apps/ai-hero/src/course-sync/control-plane.ts:42-48`) and already writes
`courseSync` provenance into resource fields
(`control-plane.ts:175-236`). Questions join that same scheme with
`kind: 'question'` and the **author-supplied `id`** as `sourceId`. Note that the
existing helper's `kind` parameter is typed `'section' | 'lesson'` and needs
widening.

What to build:

- Parse each lesson `body` for `QuizQuestion` blocks and extract the `data`
  object. Be deliberate about how: the body is MDX with JSX object literals, so
  decide between real MDX/AST parsing and something narrower, and write down why.
  A regex over JSX object literals will rot.
- Mint `targetResourceId(bindingId, 'question', <authored id>)` per question and
  write a `question` content resource, joined to its lesson through
  `contentResourceResource` with `position` preserved
  (see `packages/adapter-drizzle/.../content-resource-resource.ts:14-42`).
- Carry the full `QuestionResourceSchema` fields — including `correct` and the
  `answer` explanation — so the server can grade from the row
  (`packages/survey/src/types.ts:25-52`). `correct` may be a **string or an array
  of strings**; multi-select is required (Joel, 2026-07-25), so array values must
  survive extraction intact. Carry `allowMultiple` too.
- **Validate and fail the sync** when a question has no `id`, or when two
  questions in one lesson share an `id`. This is the loud, early failure the
  design depends on. The error must name the lesson and the offending id.
- Handle removal: a question deleted from a body should stop appearing, without
  destroying its `QuestionResponse` history. Decide soft-delete versus detach and
  say which.
- Sync is idempotent by design — re-running must not duplicate question rows or
  churn ids. The tracer run and no-op replay behavior in
  `apps/ai-hero/src/course-sync/` is the standard to match.

**Do not change the v3 manifest schema.** Quiz data rides inside the existing
`body` string; `course-json-v3.ts:86-89` rejects excess properties and that stays
true.

## Resolved when

A lesson body containing inline quizzes syncs into question content resources
with stable ids, a re-sync is a no-op, a missing or duplicate id fails the sync
with a message naming the lesson, and removing a question from a body does not
destroy collected answers.

## Result (2026-07-25)

Built on `feat/quiz-sync-extraction`, commit `d7262ba` (7 files, +563).
Reviewed and independently re-verified by the steering session.

**Parsing: real AST, not a regex.** `@mdx-js/mdx` `createProcessor` produces the
MDX AST; the extractor walks the ESTree of the `data` attribute and evaluates
only static literals. Dynamic expressions, object spreads, computed property
names, methods, and sparse arrays all throw rather than being silently mangled
(`quiz-question-extraction.ts:27-70`). Extracted objects are then validated
against `QuestionResourceSchema`. This is the durable choice the step asked for.

**Id derivation follows the existing scheme.** `targetResourceId`'s `kind` widened
to `'section' | 'lesson' | 'question'`; questions hash as
`(bindingId, 'question', <author-supplied id>)`, never the question text.

**The worker corrected the spec.** The step asked for duplicate-id detection
*within a lesson*. It implemented detection *across all lessons*, and that is
required rather than merely stricter: the id hash has no lesson component, so two
questions in different lessons sharing an authored id would collide onto one
resource row. The spec as written would have shipped that hole. The error names
both lessons.

**Removal is by relation detachment.** Question rows survive, so
`QuestionResponse` history is preserved.

**Verification.** Steering ran the tests directly: 16 passed across
`quiz-question-extraction.test.ts` (5) and `control-plane.test.ts` (11). Worker
reported 855 passing across the full suite, typecheck and course-sync ESLint
clean. Tests cover parsing, id derivation, replay idempotency, removal, rollback,
restoration, and the loud-failure paths.

The v3 manifest schema is unchanged, as required.
